  "preconditions": [
    "Explicit local/Git sources or verified unconfigured whole-project Baseline snapshots, with canonical Baseline IDs or supplied record bytes; source project identity must match."
  ],
  "steps": [
    "Acquire owned comparison sources with their actual bytes, project identity, schema and artifact-path checks; historical Baselines use only their record and archive objects.",
    "Compare Baseline pairs with the shared semantic-diff contract and independently materialized projects, preserving source bytes and existing local/Git behavior.",
    "Verify every archived object and reconstructed root, retain immutable source evidence, and reject missing/tampered bytes and unsupported opaque resource deltas. Successive Baselines compare stored history records through the same artifact diff.",
    "Reject a missing or concurrently changed native Baseline record and missing archive bytes throughout capture; preserve exact missing-object paths and host/security failures. Reject foreign projects and unsupported historical schemas; compare committed Git bytes without checkout."
  ],
  "oracle": {
    "kind": "behavior",
    "requirement_contract": "`specroad diff --against <BASE>` MUSS als Vergleichsbasis eine Baseline-ID, einen Git-Ref, ein verifiziertes Projektbundle oder ein lokales SpecRoad-Projektverzeichnis desselben Projekts akzeptieren.",
    "scope": "Owned local/Git/Baseline source registry for project configuration and artifact fields. Baseline IDs or supplied record bytes load the already supported archived whole-project snapshot and bind its verified record/root/object hashes. The same compare_sources/compare_semantic path yields the field diff. Historical archive objects are represented by their verified stored Baseline record fields; other resource bytes remain opaque and differing inventories fail. Baseline/bundle CLI discovery, complete resource semantics and full semantic validation are not claimed. Capture completion rechecks the selected native record and actual archived objects. Missing records and missing objects have distinct path-bound diagnostics; host access denial and safety violations remain errors. Legacy schema migration/readers are not inferred from current data."
  },
